# Claude Lifetime needs no configuration to run. The app is a static site and its
# database lives in the browser, so there are no secrets and no server settings.
# The variables below are optional. Copy this file to .env.local to use them.

# Path the app is served under. The portfolio serves it at /claude-lifetime.
# Set it to an empty value to serve the app at the root of a domain.
# CLAUDE_LIFETIME_BASE_PATH=/claude-lifetime

# The two variables below are used only by the Prisma CLI, which reads them from
# .env.local through prisma.config.ts. The app never reads them and never connects to a
# database server.

# Required by npm run db:migration, which prints the SQL for a change to
# prisma/schema.prisma. Prisma replays the existing migrations in this database to
# compare them with the schema, and erases everything in it each time. Point it at an
# empty PostgreSQL database that holds nothing you want to keep.
# SHADOW_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/claude_lifetime_shadow

# The database npx prisma migrate deploy applies the migrations to, if you move the
# schema to a server-side PostgreSQL.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/claude_lifetime
